{
 "summary": "The file proves three things. First, a finite nonempty family F of connected bipartite graphs, each containing a cycle, has ex(n,F) = O(n^{4/3-1/48)}, given as e(G)^16 ≤ C·n^21 for every F-free host and every n, and also in IsBigO form. Second, each member F ∈ F satisfies ex(n,F) ≥ c·n^{4/3} for all large n. Third, F is not compact, and the corrected Erdős–Simonovits compactness conjecture (∀ nonempty finite cyclic family ∃ F, C>0 with ex(n,F) ≤ C·ex(n,F) eventually) is false. The definitions match the paper's notions; the only caveats are harmless padding conjuncts (pure arithmetic facts) and a bound that is slightly stronger than the paper's (it holds for all n).",
 "glossary": [
